[{:db/id "q-211467/selection/3d8696ff4eb2a56e6c6c1dd6dd94e00a894e3dacbf8f854d5766e65b63d3f00d" :answer/id #uuid "ca2e8fe1-b567-518a-afc6-3168329e721c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3,8)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-211467/selection/e61d4285b904269a813322554976b21cde92a5afb0792125870ba07f606b195e" :answer/id #uuid "e4aa431e-69b3-5481-bb8b-f574ad755cd8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-1,8)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-211467/selection/91d27013c76788268e2e33b95f23b5af7cdbb49f9e629538a767340569105ede" :answer/id #uuid "f59f2465-d3d0-5eb3-b992-ce8b3ed21929" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-211467/selection/7898b015caa2a5b24b4c9e43acbaaa371c0f47a12e1365574e1322d58326243b" :answer/id #uuid "c6ae1596-526e-508d-93b5-68553167d632" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-211467/selection/abc4e01626eb87b45206b4cbe5fadc3db03bb1c6e9e7425dea4cb5a219c87fae" :answer/id #uuid "089092dc-a832-5d38-9cdf-4903a4a3d120" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-1,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-211467/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b5fd171c-13e2-5c92-8a60-5a006bd259bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-211467/selection/e61d4285b904269a813322554976b21cde92a5afb0792125870ba07f606b195e" :answer-field/choices ["q-211467/selection/3d8696ff4eb2a56e6c6c1dd6dd94e00a894e3dacbf8f854d5766e65b63d3f00d" "q-211467/selection/e61d4285b904269a813322554976b21cde92a5afb0792125870ba07f606b195e" "q-211467/selection/91d27013c76788268e2e33b95f23b5af7cdbb49f9e629538a767340569105ede" "q-211467/selection/7898b015caa2a5b24b4c9e43acbaaa371c0f47a12e1365574e1322d58326243b" "q-211467/selection/abc4e01626eb87b45206b4cbe5fadc3db03bb1c6e9e7425dea4cb5a219c87fae"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-211467" :question/id #uuid "75c8a190-b092-5b03-8511-92274bf3e6ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-211467" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978982/assets/d8d23cf36bc9fb526c0e6d041b72e6b378638f662b67aae63531c66b4a8cd6c5.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the local minimum and maximum of the function $y=f(x).$ What is the local maximum of $y=-f(x+2)+4?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the graph of $y=-f(x+2)+4$ can be obtained from the graph of $y=f(x)$ by \n\n- translating it by $2$ units to the left, then\n\n- flipping it across the $x$-axis, and finally\n\n- translating it by $4$ units up.\n\nSince one of these transformations flips the graph across the $x$-axis, the combined transformation maps the local **minimum** of $y=f(x)$ to the local **maximum** of $y=-f(x+2)+4.$ So, we need to find the image of $(1,-4),$ the local minimum of $y=f(x),$ under the transformation. \n\nTo plot $y=-f(x+2)+4,$ we apply the following steps: \n\n- First, we take the graph $y=f(x)$ that passes through $(1,-4).$\n\n- Then, we translate the graph by $2$ units to the left and get the graph of $y=f(x+2).$ After this transformation, the point $(1,-4)$ will be mapped to the point\n\n$$\n(1-2,-4)=(-1,-4).\n$$\n\n- Next, we flip the result across the $x$-axis and get the graph of $y=-f(x+2).$ After this transformation, the point $(-1,-4)$ will be mapped to the point\n\n$$\n(-1,-1\\cdot (-4))=(-1,4).\n$$\n\n- Finally, we translate the result by $4$ units up and get the graph of $y=-f(x+2)+4.$ After this transformation, the point $(-1,4)$ will be mapped to the point\n\n$$\n(-1,4+4)=(-1,8).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the local maximum of $y=-f(x+2)+4$ is $(-1,8).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-211467/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6eef35a-3502-5429-bd71-fb5bd0e8efc8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-211467"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-19122"] :question/problem "Let $a=⟨-1,3,2⟩$ and $b=⟨5,1,4⟩.$ Find $3a+b.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute $3a+b,$ we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a+b & =3\\cdot ⟨-1,3,2⟩+⟨5,1,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,9,6⟩+⟨5,1,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,10,10⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-112063/selection/f099982902547284f85c83c6ae9924d39b007f7b22210ccb8a3f7897f3396b99" :answer/id #uuid "62dd8bfc-4e63-5be9-abbd-1ca48ab30785" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The rate at which the area changes as the major axis changes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112063/selection/77d5e3bebedf78b9c369e205f0096be10867134c833d78ce913364699b221cf9" :answer/id #uuid "c08805e6-1136-57ee-acbb-1fd8923ea685" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The major axis of an ellipse with area S" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112063/selection/0527daa83a5fcbe40a61ce773d195fa2988e27fe798434352abe412157961698" :answer/id #uuid "f62c62f2-f8fa-5e49-8c23-99b3f1aeac51" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The rate at which the major axis changes as the minor axis changes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112063/selection/d3f484650846ef7195bec9905e3f5eeaa11a3604801e7cebe99feccfd8b53d8b" :answer/id #uuid "c375f04e-2638-5d1e-af8e-e243076948f8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The rate at which the perimeter changes as the major axis changes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112063/selection/a04eb6650840b87114d8176a0175387eff8854075ff45fd570c3c3a906c16508" :answer/id #uuid "f574a895-e26d-5f01-aaf0-c76a3f6c0a3a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The area of an ellipse with major axis $a$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112063/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "172ec8c9-c6fe-505a-aa6a-3c80be1bf22e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-112063/selection/f099982902547284f85c83c6ae9924d39b007f7b22210ccb8a3f7897f3396b99" :answer-field/choices ["q-112063/selection/f099982902547284f85c83c6ae9924d39b007f7b22210ccb8a3f7897f3396b99" "q-112063/selection/77d5e3bebedf78b9c369e205f0096be10867134c833d78ce913364699b221cf9" "q-112063/selection/0527daa83a5fcbe40a61ce773d195fa2988e27fe798434352abe412157961698" "q-112063/selection/d3f484650846ef7195bec9905e3f5eeaa11a3604801e7cebe99feccfd8b53d8b" "q-112063/selection/a04eb6650840b87114d8176a0175387eff8854075ff45fd570c3c3a906c16508"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-112063" :question/id #uuid "17829a12-d8a2-500a-8faf-3df160b9f2ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-112063" :question/problem "Consider an ellipse such that its major axis $a$ can vary while its minor axis is fixed. What is the best interpretation of ${S}^{′}(a)$ if $S$ is the area enclosed by the ellipse?" :question/worked-solution "The function $S(a)$ gives the area of the ellipse with major axis $a.$ So,\n\n$$\n{S}^{′}(a)=\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}a}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }S}{\\text{Change in }a}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${S}^{′}(a)$ is the rate at which the area changes as the major axis changes." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-112063/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "159b4d58-b34d-52cd-aad2-2c058f772ad2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-112063"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-12980/selection/448f203077738f3c0163983d9ab3c32abc607e3a13d38d26a7a160d3e1c9c545" :answer/id #uuid "a5500bcf-c7c3-5206-91f0-09dd77f547c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=35,\\,a=-4-\\sqrt{34}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12980/selection/3f5988e4c9e27ac0dd221e3021ac473944df3ec38ac6c802e75d7862c4b2a307" :answer/id #uuid "558dff4f-a12b-5f7f-a225-5bad49cfcb1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=38,\\,a=4+\\sqrt{34}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12980/selection/91757b579b41731d761f999e28399e05e29936ef78fb7d326e1da327c54fbd42" :answer/id #uuid "54e29105-bd7b-5261-a1ef-7615fbb055a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=-38,\\,a=-4\\pm \\sqrt{35}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12980/selection/fa6b05e371b85235b380fb41b897224c56383f23dc5322452e587aaf37fb2aba" :answer/id #uuid "e8a46fc1-1750-5ffa-988a-d5755e009b22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=-35,\\,a=-4\\pm \\sqrt{34}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12980/selection/2db7b389fe8d94be5582852c52cf45be33a3ac2c8563c38f8f8bffc1b4407134" :answer/id #uuid "80f9a2c4-ac98-5267-90b0-5c84f634a74b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=38,\\,a=-4\\pm \\sqrt{34}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12980/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b844afc2-b829-5d87-b161-5cbbd847b061" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-12980/selection/2db7b389fe8d94be5582852c52cf45be33a3ac2c8563c38f8f8bffc1b4407134" :answer-field/choices ["q-12980/selection/448f203077738f3c0163983d9ab3c32abc607e3a13d38d26a7a160d3e1c9c545" "q-12980/selection/3f5988e4c9e27ac0dd221e3021ac473944df3ec38ac6c802e75d7862c4b2a307" "q-12980/selection/91757b579b41731d761f999e28399e05e29936ef78fb7d326e1da327c54fbd42" "q-12980/selection/fa6b05e371b85235b380fb41b897224c56383f23dc5322452e587aaf37fb2aba" "q-12980/selection/2db7b389fe8d94be5582852c52cf45be33a3ac2c8563c38f8f8bffc1b4407134"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-12980" :question/id #uuid "614f3d78-9dad-57cb-a541-b612d5595aca" :question/math-academy-id "q-12980" :question/problem "The equation ${a}^{2}+8a=18$ can be written in the form $(a+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $p+q,$ and solve the equation." :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+8a & =18 \\\\ {a}^{2}+2\\cdot 4\\cdot a & =18 \\\\ {a}^{2}+2\\cdot a\\cdot 4+{4}^{2}-{4}^{2} & =18 \\\\ (a+4)^{2}-{4}^{2} & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a+4)^{2}-{4}^{2} & =18 \\\\ (a+4)^{2}-16 & =18 \\\\ (a+4)^{2} & =34\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $p=4,q=34,$ and $p+q=38.$\n\nNext, we solve the equation using the square-root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a+4)^{2} & =34 \\\\ \\sqrt{(a+4)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{34} \\\\ |a+4| & =\\sqrt{34} \\\\ a+4 & =\\pm \\sqrt{34} \\\\ a & =-4\\pm \\sqrt{34}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-12980/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7f04ab7-f6f6-5d01-bfcf-b667e37e4f0b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-12980"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-98013/selection/8885d985a932157a16c2ecbf3fed6fcffe83d7f2b7c450fa86db434c2b5e591b" :answer/id #uuid "e7cf9b79-fca6-5e96-808f-18c9eb14106e" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978982/assets/08925ef549329dc44ae8dc1711f101d6a2ffbbfa2c4fa225a6d21dccc458bb00.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98013/selection/f6b754b6ca8e680d253a406f79a5c519076ab52419b7a69cda372d755974a8f2" :answer/id #uuid "7d4fd306-6e7e-596c-9480-76c4c005b8b1" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978982/assets/626fbb611d42800337f0b512cdb0e221e64808ec22e0b434c3bf3c1e6d9386cc.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98013/selection/99dfa48091c7d26c5df85bb74a989745cef46694e52663d8333d21fd0a9a7f52" :answer/id #uuid "5d1d42ee-8f2f-5503-8cd6-8fb2d38da05b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978982/assets/a64e70fd5a6680fbf2ccb3236e64cbc51a014e9eecf6596d418e5a18a34fdfe6.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98013/selection/949deeedd7c273f52c0ee98b2f4d49fff766d395a1c6446183ebb6ef503ba56b" :answer/id #uuid "18823835-a7